# Sort Menu

## Summary
The picker that chooses a server-side ordering. `SortMenu` renders a list of `SortOption`s and reports the chosen one; `sortByCardTitleAsc` is the default ordering a card list falls back to. A `Sort` here is an index expression the realm evaluates, not a comparison run in the browser.

## Usage
```gts
import { SortMenu, sortByCardTitleAsc } from '@cardstack/catalog/components/sort';

<SortMenu
  @options={{this.sortOptions}}
  @selected={{this.selectedSort}}
  @onSort={{this.setSort}}
/>
```

**Not `utils/sort`.** This builds an index `Sort` expression and the picker that chooses one; `utils/sort` orders an array already in hand with a type-aware comparator. The import paths differ by one character, so read the surface rather than the name: a query that the realm runs, or an array you already hold.

## Non-goals
No comparison logic of its own — ordering is evaluated by the index, so a bespoke collation belongs in the query rather than here. No persistence of the chosen option; the consumer owns that state and passes it back in.
